<section id="S4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.3.3 </span>Single-chain</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the Single-chain tasks (Tables <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3.3 Single-chain ‣ 4.3 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SLM-Based Agentic AI with P–C–G: Optimized for Korean Tool Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3.3 Single-chain ‣ 4.3 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SLM-Based Agentic AI with P–C–G: Optimized for Korean Tool Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), P–C–G achieves a <span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Call Accuracy</span> of 95.6% and an <span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall</span> score of 91.2%, outperforming Qwen3-14B (93.0% / 88.4%) and GPT-4o-mini (86.0% / 87.4%).</p>
</div>
