</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.3.7 </span>Task Success Rate</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">According to Table <a href="#S4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ 4.3.7 Task Success Rate ‣ 4.3 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SLM-Based Agentic AI with P–C–G: Optimized for Korean Tool Use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, the proposed architecture achieves the highest TSR at <span id="S4.SS3.SSS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">79.7%</span>. While the +0.4 percentage-point improvement over GPT-4o-mini (79.3%) and EXAONE-4.0-32B-AWQ (78.6%) is not statistically significant, it remains competitive despite relying only on an SLM. It also surpasses the performance of the same base model, Qwen-8B (72.4%). These results suggest that the P–C–G design is effective with respect to task success.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T9" class="ltx_table">
